      "description": "The Abyssinian Baptist Church, located at 132 West 138th Street between Adam Clayton Powell Jr. Boulevard and Lenox Avenue in the Harlem neighborhood of Manhattan, New York City, was built in 1922-23 and was designed by Charles W. Bolton &amp; Son in Gothic Revival and Tudor Revival styles – it has also been described as \"Collegiate Gothic\". It features stained glass windows and marble furnishings The church is noted for its ministers, including Adam Clayton Powell, Sr. and Adam Clayton Powell, Jr.. (Sources: AIA Guide to NYC (5th ed.), Guide to NYC Landmarks (4th ed.) and From Anyssinian to Zion (2010))",
